# SPA fallback for Netlify.
#
# This is a client-routed app: the server has exactly one HTML file, and
# react-router decides what to render from the path. Without this rule
# Netlify looks for a file at the requested path, doesn't find one, and
# serves its 404 — so the app worked at "/" and every deep link died.
#
# It went unnoticed because normal use never requests a deep path from the
# server: you land on "/", and every route change after that is JavaScript.
# It only bites on a hard load — a bookmark, a refresh, or a link someone
# was sent. Which is exactly how a new teammate reaches /signup.
#
# 200 rather than 301: rewrite the response, don't redirect the browser, so
# the URL the user typed survives for react-router to read.
#
# Vite copies everything in public/ to the root of dist/, which is where
# Netlify expects this file.
/*  /index.html  200
